    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1108">

                <pb facs="0935" n="819" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg819"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/16755.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Belt to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hermanas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 9, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Foreign Secretary in conference this morning, when I brought up discussion of
                    recent developments, border situation, stated this question <pb facs="0936"
                        n="820" xml:id="pg820"/> would be entirely settled when the Chief Executive
                    reached Matamoros; that already arrangements had been made whereby American
                    forces could pursue bandits for a distance of fifteen leagues into Mexican
                    territory; and that Mexican soldiers would have a like privilege when in pursuit
                    of bandit bands causing trouble. He further assured me orders had been issued
                    for the Mexican Secret Service to assist the military authorities to locate and
                    punish offenders operating in vicinity of the international boundary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belt.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
